course: dictionary
lesson: 238
title: Allowance: money, limits and fairness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An allowance is an amount you are allowed. Often it is money given regularly. «Pocket money (an allowance) is regular money parents give children to learn how to handle money.» In the UK we usually say pocket money, but in the US and Canada people say allowance.
explain: An allowance can also be a limit on how much of something you may have or take. A baggage allowance is how much luggage you may take on a plane. Read the clues around the word to find out which meaning fits.
explain: «To make allowances for someone» means to be kinder or less strict because of their problems. «The Rat makes large allowances because Toad had been on prison fare» means the Rat forgives Toad because of what Toad went through. Ask: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
fact: An allowance is an amount of money given regularly, such as a weekly allowance.
fact: An allowance can also mean the amount of something you are allowed, such as a baggage allowance.
fact: «Make allowances for» means to forgive someone or be less strict because of their situation.
fact: «Daily allowance» means the amount you are allowed each day.
fact: Keep your allowance in a safe place, such as a money box or purse, and keep track of how much you have.
exercise: «Pocket money (an allowance) is regular money parents give children to learn how to handle money.» What is an allowance in this sentence? | A bag for carrying clothes on a trip | A type of prison food | A kind of punishment | *Regular money given to a child
exercise: A baggage allowance is the amount of luggage you are allowed to take on a plane. What does baggage allowance mean? | A map of the airport | *The amount of luggage you are allowed to take | The price of a plane ticket | A list of bags you must leave behind
exercise: «The Rat makes large allowances because Toad had been on prison fare.» What does make large allowances mean here? | Gives Toad a huge meal | Locks Toad in a cell | *Forgives Toad because of what he went through | Charges Toad a large fee
test: Where does the text suggest you keep your pocket money safe? | Given to a stranger for keeping | Spent on the first day | Under the bed, out in the open | *In a money box or purse
test: Mia has a daily allowance of two snacks. What does daily allowance mean? | The money you owe each day | The time of day when snacks are sold | A snack you make yourself each morning | *The amount you are allowed each day
exam: Which sentence uses allowance to mean money given regularly? | «The plane has a baggage allowance of twenty kilograms.» | «The Rat makes large allowances for Toad.» | «Your allowance is worth keeping safe, but not in a box.» | *«Pocket money, also called an allowance, is a small regular amount that parents give children.»
